          dealing: 'Players get no hands. All 28 tiles are dealt face down into a grid layout of 4 by 7 tiles.',
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Be the first player to reach 50 captured tiles (25 pairs), or another predetermined total, by turning up pairs of tiles that total 12.',
          gameplay: '1. Setup: all 28 tiles are placed face down in a 4×7 grid. 2. On your turn, expose any two tiles. If the pair totals 12, remove them from the grid and take another turn (continue until you fail to get a total of 12). If the pair does not total 12, turn them face down again and the next player takes a turn. 3. The hand is over when the grid is empty. 4. Winner is the first to reach 50 captured tiles (25 pairs) or the agreed total.',
          keyRules: [
            'Each turn: expose two tiles. If they total 12, remove them and go again; otherwise turn them face down and pass the turn.',
            'Domino pairs that total 12: double-six with double-blank, 5-6 with 0-1; any seven (e.g. 1-6, 2-5, 3-4) pairs with any five (0-5, 1-4, 2-3) for nine combinations.',
            'Game ends when grid is empty. First to 50 tiles (25 pairs) or agreed total wins.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Remember which tiles appeared where when they were turned face down so you can form pairs that total 12 on your turn.',
          intermediate: 'Remember the total (12) and think in terms of pairs of values (e.g. 7 and 5) rather than the two halves of each tile.',
          advanced: 'Dominoes do not break into simple pairs like cards: double-blank and double-six pair only with each other; 0-1 and 5-6 pair only with each other. For 7+5 there are nine tile combinations (1-6, 2-5, or 3-4 with 0-5, 1-4, or 2-3); use this to plan which positions to reveal.',
          tips: [
            'Concentrate on the total 12 and the positions of turned-down tiles.',
            'Avoid confusing the two ends of a tile; remember the sum each tile contributes.',
            'When several tiles can make 12 with the same partner, track positions so you do not waste a turn on a wrong pair.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
